What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Isaac J. Manjarres <isaacmanjarres@google.com>
Description:
		/sys/kernel/ashmem/ contains a single node that can be used
		to adjust different characteristics of the ashmem driver's
		behavior.

What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/unpinning_enable
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Isaac J. Manjarres <isaacmanjarres@google.com>
Description:
		Can be used to configure if ashmem's memory unpinning feature
		is enabled.

		A value of 0 indicates that the feature is disabled.

		When the unpinning feature is disabled, unpin requests are
		nops, and the ashmem shrinker will not run.

		A value of 1 indicates that the feature is enabled, and
		operating as expected.

What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/ignore_unset_prot_read
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Isaac J. Manjarres <isaacmanjarres@google.com>
Description:
		Can be used to control if ashmem allows clients to remove
		PROT_READ from a buffer's mapping permissions set.

		A value of 0 indicates that ashmem will allow a client to
		remove PROT_READ from a buffer's mapping permissions set.

		A value of 1 will silently ignore the request to remove
		PROT_READ.

What:		/sys/kernel/ashmem/ignore_unset_prot_exec
Date:		Feb 2025
Contact:	Isaac J. Manjarres <isaacmanjarres@google.com>
Description:
		Can be used to control if ashmem allows clients to remove
		PROT_EXEC from a buffer's mapping permissions set.

		A value of 0 indicates that ashmem will allow a client to
		remove PROT_EXEC from a buffer's mapping permissions set.

		A value of 1 will silently ignore the request to remove
		PROT_EXEC.
